course: dictionary
lesson: 14656
title: Predominance: the most of them
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Predominance is a formal noun. It means that one thing is greater in number or more common than the others. It can also mean that one group has the most power or influence. «A predominance of girls in the choir» means there are more girls than any other kind of singer.
explain: Look for the clue words. Predominance often comes with «of», as in «a predominance of» or «the predominance of». When you meet it, try putting «most» or «more» in its place. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: The word appears in different lessons. In maths or geography, it can describe which group is biggest in a set of data, such as a bar chart of favourite colours. In history, it can describe which country or group had the most power, such as «the predominance of one empire».
fact: Predominance is a noun, and it is a formal word.
fact: «Predominance» means being more in number or more common than others.
fact: «Predominance» can also mean having the most power or influence.
fact: Useful phrases are «a predominance of», «the predominance of» and «in predominance».
fact: A quick check: swap in «most» or «more» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «There was a predominance of red cars in the car park.» What does predominance mean here? | Cars that do not work | *More of them than other colours | Fast cars | A very old car park
exercise: In history, «the predominance of one empire» means what? | A map with no names | *The most power or influence | The smallest group of people | A long and boring book
exercise: Which word usually comes after predominance in the phrases we learned? | Quickly | Under | Blue | *of
test: «In our class, there is a predominance of readers who love fantasy books.» What does predominance mean? | Very angry readers | Very quiet | *More of them than others, the most common | A short list
test: Which phrase means the same as predominance in «the predominance of one team in the league»? | Being the last team | Having no rules at all | Winning a prize for art | *Having the most power or influence
exam: «The map shows a predominance of green fields in the south.» What does predominance mean? | A type of map | Fields that are dry and brown | A small green hill | *Most common or in greatest number
